  "extractionNotes": "Grant evidenced by the maternity-benefit title on the ZUS account (2025-03-18..2026-03-16) with a handwritten ZUS remark that the right was granted; no decision text. The ZAM (dated 2025-03-24, 6 days after the birth, full-length declaration ticked) splits the 52 weeks into maternity to 2025-08-04 and parental from 2025-08-05; the split is the claim. Employment title from 2023-09-21 on both the ZUS screen and the Z-3. Employer remark: working time raised from 1/2 to full time on 2024-08-01; first incapacity 2024-09-17 (employer sick pay 5 days), then e-ZLA pregnancy notes (code B; one note shows a two-letter code, omitted) from 2024-10-08 to 2025-03-25, overlapping the birth. Only one full month after the change precedes the incapacity, so the Z-3 lists only 2024-08 (4300.00 = the minimum wage); maternity follows sickness without a gap, so that base carries over. Base 3710.47 and daily 100.80 at 81.5% are our computation, reported only. ZUS sick-pay and sickness-benefit amounts are not in the file."
